  "id": "time-estimation",
  "term": "time estimation",
  "definition": "Time estimation is the mental process of judging how much time has passed or how long an interval lasts. In the source material, it is described as a form of subjective timing that is often treated as scaling with objective clock time, with variability tending to increase as the duration being judged gets longer.",
